===============================================================================
SPEC OBSERVATIONS RAISED BY THIS BUILD (all now resolved in the spec)
===============================================================================

[S1] RESOLVED -> new clause 3.3 item 1b VACUOUS-CONTAIN.
     Reported: the 3.1 clip uses w_lo = min(w(t0),w(t1)) and is the only clause that
     consults containment, but admissibility needs cx >= w(t)/2 POINTWISE. Near t in
     {0,1}, w_lo = 1 while w(t) > 1 in the interior, so the clipped box keeps placements
     with cx in [1/2, w(t)/2) that leave [0,s]^2. Splitting t never helps (any
     subinterval retaining t=0 or t=1 still has w_lo=1) -> infinite regress -> cap FAIL.
     Measured on pair_smoke_paths: stuck box F t=[0.995278,1] x=[511/512,257/256]
     y=[1/2,131/256]; at t=256/257, centre (511/512,1/2) the E3- quadratic has
     A=257/512, B=-1, C=255/512, so 4AC-B^2 = -4/262144 < 0 with interior vertex - the
     square is genuinely core-separated (~4e-6) while reaching y=-0.0019, i.e. not
     container-admissible and not a real obligation.
     Implemented per the new 1b: exact endpoint-only test per side, e.g. left violated
     for all placements iff (x1+1/2)t^2 - t + (x1-1/2) < 0 at BOTH t0 and t1 (positive
     leading coefficient => the sup over the interval is at an endpoint).
     Selftest coverage: 2500-draw fuzz vs float containment sampling (0 soundness
     violations, predicate fired 1135x) PLUS two unit assertions, because a clause that
     never fires would pass a fuzz vacuously - and it fires 0 times on the whole corpus.

[S2] RESOLVED -> 4 hint schema now carries failing SETS.
     Reported: 4 still specified a scalar sigma per witness while 3.6 had moved to
     failing sets, which 3.6 itself calls the norm near axis orientations (size 2).
     This build re-derives COVERED/COVERED_F from scratch, so witness payloads are
     advisory; the parser now validates the failing-SET shape so a hint written against
     the superseded scalar schema is reported as version skew (hint_miss) rather than
     silently ignored.

[S3] ACCEPTED as implemented. Gates (a)/(b) of 5.4 name the toy PASS cert, but
     pair_toy_s199 has an EMPTY atom list (PASS is by NONDISJOINT), so halving or
     deleting an atom is a no-op there; nor can a mass-load-bearing PASS cert exist at
     toy scale (obligations begin at exactly s=2, the tangency case 8 calls
     uncertifiable). Gates are applied to the COVERED clause directly, per the v1
     precedent. The A73 anchors now supply the mass-load-bearing PASS path and are wired
     into the selftest corpus.

[S4] Smoke has no v1 report, so its verdict cannot be cross-validated against v1; the
     agreed criterion is AGREEMENT between the two v2 implementations. Both report FAIL
     with a cap witness at comparable budgets.

[S5] Lemma M pinning (3.4) confirmed by independent derivation:
     du/dcx = -C <= 0, du/dcy = -S <= 0, dv/dcx = +S >= 0, dv/dcy = -C <= 0 on t in
     [0,1], so the SLACK-minimising corners are g1@(x0,y0), g2@(x1,y1), g3@(x1,y0),
     g4@(x0,y1) exactly as written.

SPLIT HEURISTIC (6) - two gates, both found by cross-validation against the reference:
  (i)  possible-collectability: only atoms possibly collectable in BOTH factors are
       eligible targets (each constraint's max over the box >= 0, pinned at the corner
       OPPOSITE Lemma M's min corner, via Lemma Q's max analogue).
  (ii) weight-per-needed-shrink, not weight alone: a tangentially-reachable atom has a
       pinned min stuck at e.g. -1/4 regardless of how t is halved, so ranking by weight
       alone chases it forever while x and y collapse for vanishing gains. Ranking by
       w / (needed shrink) demotes it.
  Plus: a dimension's halving must close >= 1% of the remaining gap to be chosen;
  otherwise the v1 widest-dimension rule (tscale 2) takes over and guarantees progress.
  Before these: anchor_grid06 thrashed to depth 40 in 50 nodes with cov=0. After:
  grid05 PASS in 23782 nodes (max_depth 26), grid06 PASS in 514 (max_depth 6).
  Reference node counts are 5866 and 1098; 3.2 Lemma S makes soundness independent of
  the split rule, so counts are free to differ.

COMPLETENESS-ONLY IMPLEMENTATION LIMITS (never affect soundness; all make PASS harder):
  - COVERED-F greedy caps: <= 12 MEM and <= 6 EXC witnesses per node, failing sets of
    size <= 4, <= 512 atoms evaluated per node.
  - COVERED-F witness candidates are drawn from the certain-membership shortlist.
  - The float pre-screen skips atoms already PROVEN (via an endpoint value of a pinned
    slack quadratic, which upper-bounds its minimum) to fail more than 4 constraints.
